# app/elohim-library — shared libraries and pattern libraries

What belongs here: libraries and stories scoped to client concerns (UX, accessibility, and
sense-and-respond), composed from exactly three sources. Those are the ts-rs generated views,
the app-manifest vocabulary, and the graphos design tokens (`CLAUDE.md`, "The three sources of
truth"). A story that invents a local interface, hardcodes a brand colour, or uses vocabulary
outside the manifest is wrong. component-architect writes Library A; graphos-designer writes
Library B; neither crosses into the other's.

`covers: subtree` is a considered ownership claim with no edit-time rule. The drifts that matter
here are content-shaped (thin-client scope, the Library A/B boundary), so review and the render
rails (`pnpm graphos sheet`) hold them. A committed build artefact such as
`projects/*/coverage/` is a `.gitignore` concern; the resolver never sees those writes.
